From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:53:04 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-ps1

PlayStation gets its own shelf, Games/PS1, on pcsx_rearmed alone, with every
platform policy answered explicitly and its own Screen section (a Shader row
on the retro list, stored in Config/ps1_shader.txt, and a Picture row,
Actual by default, then Stretch, no Crop). Discs are .cue, .chd, .pbp and
.m3u; a .bin is never a game. A playlist hides the discs it names, read the
way pcsx reads it, and (Disc N) or (Disc N of M) files with no playlist
become one game with a playlist written to Config/playlists/PS1. A playlist
that names a missing disc or more than 8 discs is refused before the core
sees it. The disc serial and its region are read from SYSTEM.CNF for the
case art later. The shelf shows a placeholder GBA shape until the jewel
cases land.

The grouping and the playlist rules follow AaronC1990/tray and
oauramos/omega-zero, and the generated PS-X EXE and ISO test fixture is
ported from bently0602/slot (all GPL-3.0).
